<h1>Welcome to the Wallaby Admin Demo site</h1>
<%= render 'flash_messages' %>
<p>Data on this site is regenerated daily using the <code>FFaker</code> gem. Please do not save sensitive information here.</p>
<p>If you're interested, check out the demo repository at <a href="https://github.com/wallaby-rails/wallaby-demo" target="_blank">https://github.com/wallaby-rails/wallaby-demo</a>.</p>
<h4>What to check out:</h4>
<ul>
  <li>Check out how Wallaby handles models with a non-standard primary key (e.g., <%= index_link SchemaMigration %>).</li>
  <li>Check out all the PostgreSQL data types that Wallaby supports on the <%= index_link AllPostgresType %> model pages (
    <%= index_link(AllPostgresType) { 'index' } %> /
    <%= show_link(AllPostgresType.first) { 'show' } %> /
    <%= edit_link(AllPostgresType.first, html_options: { class: '' }) { 'edit' } %> ).
  </li>
  <li>
    Check out how associations are displayed on index and show pages, and autocompleted on forms (e.g., the <%= new_link(Product, html_options: { class: '' }) { 'Product create page' } %>):
    <ul>
      <li><code>belongs_to</code>: a <%= index_link Product %> belongs to a <%= index_link Category %>, and an <%= index_link Order::Item %> belongs to an <%= index_link Order %>.</li>
      <li><code>has_one</code>: a <%= index_link User %> has one <%= index_link Profile %>.</li>
      <li><code>has_many</code>: a <%= index_link Product %> has many <%= index_link Order %>s, and many <%= index_link Order::Item %>s through <%= index_link Order %>s.</li>
      <li><code>has_and_belongs_to_many</code>: a <%= index_link Product %> has and belongs to many <%= index_link Tag %>s.</li>
      <li><code>polymorphic</code>: a <%= index_link Picture %> belongs to imageables (e.g., a <%= index_link Product %>, a <%= index_link User %>, and a <%= index_link Category %>).</li>
      <li><code>STI (single table inheritance)</code>: <%= index_link User %>, <%= index_link SuperUser %>, and <%= index_link Operator %> are the STI types for the <code>users</code> table.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>Check out how Active Storage is handled for the <%= index_link Picture %> model.</li>
</ul>
